From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] cambium-ab: refuse the deprecated untested conversion override

Unsupported models must not reach flash or environment operations. Reject the
old override before sourcing runtime libraries; keep normal verified conversion
and resume options intact. This is not the unified OEM migration path.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/package/cambium/cambium-ab/files/cambium-ab-convert
+++ b/package/cambium/cambium-ab/files/cambium-ab-convert
@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@
 # running bank must hold a valid device-data vault (filled from the OEM slot
 # at first boot), and the boot environment must already boot the running
 # bank first. The OEM image value is kept as ${AB_ENV}_ab_oem_image.
+
+for argument in "$@"; do
+ case "$argument" in
+ --allow-untested)
+  echo 'cambium-ab-convert: --allow-untested is no longer supported; use a reviewed exact-model path' >&2
+  exit 2 ;;
+ esac
+done
 
 . "${CAMBIUM_SYSTEM_FUNCTIONS:-/lib/functions/system.sh}"
 . "${CAMBIUM_AB_LIB:-/lib/functions/cambium-ab.sh}"
